00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:57.440
they're doing and will also have to report back&nbsp;
to these npcs once the objectives are completed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:01.600
the souls games also love to draw inspiration&nbsp;
from specific media and bloodborne took this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:06.160
a step further by making hp lovecraft and his&nbsp;
lovecraftian stories be the inspiration for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:10.800
game's plot and while sekiro does do this as well&nbsp;
instead of fully embracing the fictional elements&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:15.360
of h.p lovecraft like with bloodborne sekiro goes&nbsp;
in the opposite direction and instead focuses on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:20.480
non-fiction storytelling by using history culture&nbsp;
and religion all of these decisions are very bold&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:24.720
especially coming from a game series that likes to&nbsp;
stick to what it knows best this further added to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:28.720
the attraction of the game as this was something&nbsp;
the soul series has never done before however one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:33.280
of these decisions being the history and culture&nbsp;
surrounding the game will become an issue to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:38.160
explain why we need to recap that intro again with&nbsp;
the proper context as I said this game takes place&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:43.360
in the sengoku era of japan which was a real time&nbsp;
period in japan's history it was an over 100 year&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:47.520
conflict that started because the shogunate at&nbsp;
